"}}}
{"qid": "c02", "family": "c", "split": "dev", "method": "M3", "model": "glm", "answer": {"method": "M3", "model": "glm", "final": {"answer": "The item directly upstream of CHV-2-2 is FV-2-2, the flow control valve in loop FIC-2-2 (the ActuatingFunction for FIC-2-2 controls FV-2-2, and FV-2-2 sends flow on line PL-10 into CHV-2-2). FV-2-2's datasheet is fisher-et-d100022x012, the Fisher ET product bulletin. According to that datasheet, a Fisher ET is a sliding-stem control valve: it is a single-port, globe-style valve body with cage guiding, a balanced valve plug, and push-down-to-close plug action, used for throttling or on-off control of liquids and gases. So yes, it is the valve body of a globe-style (sliding-stem) control valve, part of the Fisher easy-e family (with EAT the angle version and ETR the push-down-to-open version).", "not_present": false}, "outcome": "ANSWERED", "route": ["context_rag+chunks"], "cypher": [], "sources": [{"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "pages": [29, 36, 1, 8, 9, 16, 31, 3, 2, 22, 4]}, {"document_id": "flowserve-worcester-f51-f52", "pages": [11]}], "latency_s": 2.016496800002642, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 14640, "completion_tokens": 344, "cost_usd": 0.00119854, "spent_usd": 0.00119854, "n_calls": 2, "n_cached": 0, "models": ["qwen/qwen3-embedding-8b", "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash"]}, "trace": {"chunks": [{"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 29, "score": 0.6535}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 36, "score": 0.6516}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 1, "score": 0.6384}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 8, "score": 0.6342}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 9, "score": 0.6054}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 16, "score": 0.6015}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 31, "score": 0.599}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 3, "score": 0.5886}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 2, "score": 0.5866}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 22, "score": 0.5773}, {"document_id": "flowserve-worcester-f51-f52", "page": 11, "score": 0.574}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 4, "score": 0.5728}], "prompt_chars": 38774, "reply": "{\"answer\": \"The item directly upstream of CHV-2-2 is FV-2-2, the flow control valve in loop FIC-2-2 (the ActuatingFunction for FIC-2-2 controls FV-2-2, and FV-2-2 sends flow on line PL-10 into CHV-2-2). FV-2-2's datasheet is fisher-et-d100022x012, the Fisher ET product bulletin. According to that datasheet, a Fisher ET is a sliding-stem control valve: it is a single-port, globe-style valve body with cage guiding, a balanced valve plug, and push-down-to-close plug action, used for throttling or on-off control of liquids and gases. So yes, it is the valve body of a globe-style (sliding-stem) control valve, part of the Fisher easy-e family (with EAT the angle version and ETR the push-down-to-open version).\", \"not_present\": false}"}}}
{"qid": "c03", "family": "c", "split": "dev", "method": "M3", "model": "glm", "answer": {"method": "M3", "model": "glm", "final": {"answer": "The transmitter feeding FIC-2-2 is FT-2-2, covered by the Rosemount 3051 datasheet (rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001). When self-diagnostics detect a sensor or microprocessor failure, the analog output is driven either high or low to alert the user; the default is NAMUR-compliant levels (high alarm ≥ 22.5 mA, low alarm ≤ 3.6 mA). Whether the failure drives the signal high or low is user-selectable with a jumper/switch on the transmitter. In addition, the alarm direction/levels can be specified at order time via the alarm levels option codes: C4 (NAMUR alarm high), CN (NAMUR alarm low), or CR/CS for custom high/low alarm and saturation levels (which require the C1 custom software configuration option).", "not_present": false}, "outcome": "ANSWERED", "route": ["context_rag+chunks"], "cypher": [], "sources": [{"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "pages": [88, 15, 109, 46, 35, 86, 83, 57, 62, 74, 26, 42]}], "latency_s": 2.2288388999877498, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 12712, "completion_tokens": 360, "cost_usd": 0.00097348, "spent_usd": 0.00097348, "n_calls": 2, "n_cached": 0, "models": ["qwen/qwen3-embedding-8b", "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash"]}, "trace": {"chunks": [{"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 88, "score": 0.5841}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 15, "score": 0.5226}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 109, "score": 0.5218}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 46, "score": 0.5168}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 35, "score": 0.5164}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 86, "score": 0.5066}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 83, "score": 0.5065}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 57, "score": 0.4993}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 62, "score": 0.4971}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 74, "score": 0.4939}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 26, "score": 0.49}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 42, "score": 0.4869}], "prompt_chars": 37015, "reply": "{\"answer\": \"The transmitter feeding FIC-2-2 is FT-2-2, covered by the Rosemount 3051 datasheet (rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001). When self-diagnostics detect a sensor or microprocessor failure, the analog output is driven either high or low to alert the user; the default is NAMUR-compliant levels (high alarm ≥ 22.5 mA, low alarm ≤ 3.6 mA). Whether the failure drives the signal high or low is user-selectable with a jumper/switch on the transmitter. In addition, the alarm direction/levels can be specified at order time via the alarm levels option codes: C4 (NAMUR alarm high), CN (NAMUR alarm low), or CR/CS for custom high/low alarm and saturation levels (which require the C1 custom software configuration option).\", \"not_present\": false}"}}}
{"qid": "c04", "family": "c", "split": "dev", "method": "M3", "model": "glm", "answer": {"method": "M3", "model": "glm", "final": {"answer": null, "not_present": true}, "outcome": "ANSWERED", "route": ["context_rag+chunks"], "cypher": [], "sources": [{"document_id": "gorman-rupp-0700286", "pages": [2, 4, 3, 5, 6]}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "pages": [32, 93, 106]}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "pages": [36, 29]}, {"document_id": "flowserve-worcester-f51-f52", "pages": [12, 11]}], "latency_s": 1.7931471000192687, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 12328, "completion_tokens": 96, "cost_usd": 0.0008271999999999999, "spent_usd": 0.0008271999999999999, "n_calls": 2, "n_cached": 0, "models": ["qwen/qwen3-embedding-8b", "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash"]}, "trace": {"chunks": [{"document_id": "gorman-rupp-0700286", "page": 2, "score": 0.5469}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 32, "score": 0.541}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 36, "score": 0.5351}, {"document_id": "gorman-rupp-0700286", "page": 4, "score": 0.5251}, {"document_id": "gorman-rupp-0700286", "page": 3, "score": 0.5186}, {"document_id": "gorman-rupp-0700286", "page": 5, "score": 0.5158}, {"document_id": "gorman-rupp-0700286", "page": 6, "score": 0.5156}, {"document_id": "flowserve-worcester-f51-f52", "page": 12, "score": 0.5087}, {"document_id": "flowserve-worcester-f51-f52", "page": 11, "score": 0.4975}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 29, "score": 0.496}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 93, "score": 0.4943}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 106, "score": 0.4938}], "prompt_chars": 31809, "reply": "{\"answer\": null, \"not_present\": true}"}}}
{"qid": "c05", "family": "c", "split": "dev", "method": "M3", "model": "glm", "answer": {"method": "M3", "model": "glm", "final": {"answer": "The item directly downstream of E-2-1 in the process flow is FV-2-2, a globe valve on line PL-10 (the Fisher ET control valve, per the fisher-et-d100022x012 datasheet). Its available seal and ring materials and temperature capabilities are: 2-piece valve plug seal with a PTFE disk (-73 to 204 °C / -100 to 400 °F) and backup ring in fluorocarbon (-18 to 204 °C / 0 to 400 °F), ethylene-propylene (-40 to 232 °C / -40 to 450 °F), or nitrile (-40 to 71 °C / -40 to 160 °F for air and hydrocarbons, -40 to 82 °C / -40 to 180 °F for other compatible fluids); a seal ring of carbon-filled PTFE (-73 to 232 °C / -100 to 450 °F); and a spring-loaded valve plug seal with a PTFE seal ring and N10276 spring (-73 to 232 °C / -100 to 450 °F) or a PTFE/graphite seal ring with R30003 spring (-73 to 316 °C / -100 to 600 °F), with PEEK (polyetheretherketone) anti-extrusion rings available to extend use above 232 °C / 450 °F up to 316 °C / 600 °F in non-oxidizing service (260 °C / 500 °F in oxidizing service).", "not_present": false}, "outcome": "ANSWERED", "route": ["context_rag+chunks"], "cypher": [], "sources": [{"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "pages": [22, 12, 4, 20, 5, 2, 14, 21, 11, 7]}, {"document_id": "flowserve-worcester-f51-f52", "pages": [7]}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "pages": [68]}], "latency_s": 7.1488959999987856, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 17597, "completion_tokens": 573, "cost_usd": 0.00164084, "spent_usd": 0.00164084, "n_calls": 2, "n_cached": 0, "models": ["qwen/qwen3-embedding-8b", "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash"]}, "trace": {"chunks": [{"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 22, "score": 0.7017}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 12, "score": 0.6793}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 4, "score": 0.6732}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 20, "score": 0.6718}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 5, "score": 0.6639}, {"document_id": "flowserve-worcester-f51-f52", "page": 7, "score": 0.663}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 2, "score": 0.6623}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 14, "score": 0.6556}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 21, "score": 0.6548}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 68, "score": 0.6496}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 11, "score": 0.6465}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 7, "score": 0.6451}], "prompt_chars": 47588, "reply": "{\"answer\": \"The item directly downstream of E-2-1 in the process flow is FV-2-2, a globe valve on line PL-10 (the Fisher ET control valve, per the fisher-et-d100022x012 datasheet). Its available seal and ring materials and temperature capabilities are: 2-piece valve plug seal with a PTFE disk (-73 to 204 °C / -100 to 400 °F) and backup ring in fluorocarbon (-18 to 204 °C / 0 to 400 °F), ethylene-propylene (-40 to 232 °C / -40 to 450 °F), or nitrile (-40 to 71 °C / -40 to 160 °F for air and hydrocarbons, -40 to 82 °C / -40 to 180 °F for other compatible fluids); a seal ring of carbon-filled PTFE (-73 to 232 °C / -100 to 450 °F); and a spring-loaded valve plug seal with a PTFE seal ring and N10276 spring (-73 to 232 °C / -100 to 450 °F) or a PTFE/graphite seal ring with R30003 spring (-73 to 316 °C / -100 to 600 °F), with PEEK (polyetheretherketone) anti-extrusion rings available to extend use above 232 °C / 450 °F up to 316 °C / 600 °F in non-oxidizing service (260 °C / 500 °F in oxidizing service).\", \"not_present\": false}"}}}
{"qid": "d01", "family": "d", "split": "dev", "method": "M3", "model": "glm", "answer": {"method": "M3", "model": "glm", "final": {"answer": "GV-1-2 is a globe valve served by the GFPS Type 165 2/2-way solenoid valve datasheet, and a humming coil that fails to open points to a few causes described there. The valve is servo-controlled and requires a minimum differential pressure of 0.5 bar to open and close, so if the pressure differential across it is below 0.5 bar it will energize (hum) but not open. The datasheet also specifies the media must be clean liquids without solid particles, so debris or particles in the line could be blocking or jamming the diaphragm/insert so the pilot cannot actuate. Additionally, the supply voltage must be within the stated tolerance of ±10% (24V DC, 230V or 115V 50/60 Hz depending on the coil fitted); an out-of-tolerance or wrong-voltage supply can leave the coil humming without enough force to shift the valve. Checking the differential pressure, media cleanliness, and coil voltage against the datasheet's technical data would be the appropriate troubleshooting steps.", "not_present": false}, "outcome": "ANSWERED", "route": ["context_rag+chunks"], "cypher": [], "sources": [{"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "pages": [36, 1, 3]}, {"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "pages": [3, 1, 6, 2, 5, 4]}, {"document_id": "flowserve-worcester-f51-f52", "pages": [10, 1]}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "pages": [42]}], "latency_s": 2.8254399000434205, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 12514, "completion_tokens": 436, "cost_usd": 0.0009477, "spent_usd": 0.0009477, "n_calls": 2, "n_cached": 0, "models": ["qwen/qwen3-embedding-8b", "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash"]}, "trace": {"chunks": [{"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 36, "score": 0.6394}, {"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "page": 3, "score": 0.5967}, {"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "page": 1, "score": 0.5688}, {"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "page": 6, "score": 0.5609}, {"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "page": 2, "score": 0.5502}, {"document_id": "flowserve-worcester-f51-f52", "page": 10, "score": 0.5469}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 1, "score": 0.54}, {"document_id": "flowserve-worcester-f51-f52", "page": 1, "score": 0.5371}, {"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "page": 5, "score": 0.5363}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 3, "score": 0.5305}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 42, "score": 0.5297}, {"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "page": 4, "score": 0.5273}], "prompt_chars": 33418, "reply": "{\"answer\": \"GV-1-2 is a globe valve served by the GFPS Type 165 2/2-way solenoid valve datasheet, and a humming coil that fails to open points to a few causes described there. The valve is servo-controlled and requires a minimum differential pressure of 0.5 bar to open and close, so if the pressure differential across it is below 0.5 bar it will energize (hum) but not open. The datasheet also specifies the media must be clean liquids without solid particles, so debris or particles in the line could be blocking or jamming the diaphragm/insert so the pilot cannot actuate. Additionally, the supply voltage must be within the stated tolerance of ±10% (24V DC, 230V or 115V 50/60 Hz depending on the coil fitted); an out-of-tolerance or wrong-voltage supply can leave the coil humming without enough force to shift the valve. Checking the differential pressure, media cleanliness, and coil voltage against the datasheet's technical data would be the appropriate troubleshooting steps.\", \"not_present\": false}"}}}
